2.steps:
1.Login firewall and go to Network/DNS page;
2.Check that by default, the option Inherit DNS Settings Dynamically from the WAN Zone is selected;
3.Select the radio button Specify DNS Servers Manually, enter following value for all the three dns servers and click the Accept button;
256.1.1.1 1.256.1.1 1.1.1.256 1.1.@.1 1.1.1.-9 Asfdfds 10.10.10.10

8.steps:
1.Restore firewall to factory default;
2.Configure wan interface, select static mode,configure DNS servers on the page;
3.Go to Network->DNS, check that the dns servers all inherit from wan settings page;
4.Change wan interface to different mode like DHCP, pppoe,l2tp and pptp, when it connects to the corresponding server correctly, do step3.

4.steps:
1. Fill a real dns server as server1, then fill two fake dns servers as server 2 and server 3;
2. Initiate a dns query and capture the packets, dns query should forward to the server1 and it should reply with the correct IP address;
3. Fill a fake dns server as server1 and server3, fill a real dns as server2, do step2 again;
4. Fill a fake dns server as server1 and server2, fill a real dns as server3, do step2 again;

